{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe mean reversion lag: The model consistently underestimates the magnitude of upward spikes (e.g., rising from ~68 to ~80) and fails to anticipate the subsequent sharp decline, treating volatile trends as linear continuations.",
    "Apply aggressive downward correction after sentiment spikes: When sentiment history shows positive signals (0.20-0.33) coinciding with price surges, the model's forecast is too conservative; immediately reduce the forecast by 10-15% to account for the inevitable post-spike crash.",
    "Adjust for overshoot in the mid-horizon (days 10-20): The model predicts a slow, steady recovery or plateau, but true outcomes show a rapid drop to lower baselines (60-65 range) after the peak; force a steeper negative slope in the forecast for the second half of the 30-day window.",
    "Ignore flat sentiment baselines during volatility: When sentiment is 0.00, do not assume stability; the model's flat-line forecasts are systematically wrong during high-volatility regimes and must be adjusted to reflect the observed oscillation amplitude.",
    "Calibrate for terminal value decay: The model forecasts a gradual increase to ~73, while actuals drop to ~62; apply a terminal correction factor of -10 to the final 5-day forecast horizon."
  ]
}
